newspaper-demo-name = WASTELAND HERALD
newspaper-demo-headline = CARAVAN VANISHES ON OLD HIGHWAY
newspaper-demo-lead = The last signal came at dawn. What we know so far
newspaper-demo-body = Yesterday the caravan failed to reach its camp. Residents found wheel tracks on the road, but no survivors.

    The editorial desk is gathering witness accounts and asks for reports of any signals from the highway.
newspaper-demo-brieftitle = Clean water returns to the market
newspaper-demo-briefbody = Deliveries resumed after the pump was repaired.
newspaper-demo-notetitle = Radio tower is transmitting again
newspaper-demo-notebody = Who is on air and which frequency should listeners tune to?
newspaper-demo-backbody = The caravan left in the morning and was expected to reach the settlement before dark. Two traders saw it on the last stretch of the road. They say the convoy kept moving without stopping.

    Wheel tracks were later found near the old highway. Their destination remains unclear: sand has covered part of the road.

    The editorial desk seeks anyone who heard the caravan's final radio exchange. Leave reports at the desk or send them on air.
newspaper-demo-brief2title = Lights spotted near the highway
newspaper-demo-brief2body = Caravan traders ask witnesses to come forward.
newspaper-demo-radioschedule = Today on air

    19:00 — news report
    20:00 — residents' voices
    21:00 — notices
newspaper-demo-radiostation = TUNE TO 1728
    Voice of the Wasteland
newspaper-demo-teasertitle = Traders seek an escort
newspaper-demo-teaserbody = Details and meeting location inside.
newspaper-demo-announcements = A caravan needs guides. Meet at the south gate in the morning.

    The workshop buys generator repair parts.
newspaper-demo-photocaption = Old highway. Photo by the editorial correspondent.
newspaper-demo-callouttitle = Have information? Contact the editorial desk
newspaper-demo-calloutbody = We accept photos, letters and witness accounts.
newspaper-demo-backheadline = What happened on the old highway
newspaper-demo-backlead = Witness accounts, the final route and unanswered questions
newspaper-demo-quote = They passed us before sunset.
newspaper-demo-quoteauthor = — a trader on the northern route
newspaper-demo-backsecondarytitle = The final signal
newspaper-demo-backsecondarybody = Contact was lost shortly after the convoy passed the junction.

    The radio host asks listeners to report any recording or memory of the transmission.

    New information will appear in the next edition.
newspaper-demo-backothertitle = Radio tower is back in service
newspaper-demo-backotherbody = The signal can be heard in the surrounding area. Operators are seeking a stable frequency for the evening news.
